.DS_Store
*.log

# Python bytecode. scripts/check_homepage.py and scripts/capability_strip.py
# import generate_matrix as a module, so every build writes a .pyc here. One got
# committed twice before this rule existed — both times by a `git add -A` after
# a build, which is exactly how a generated file sneaks into a repo.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Scratch pages served out of docs/ while measuring rendered output. They are
# written into the built site so a local server can reach them, which puts them
# one `git add -A` away from being published.
docs/_*

# Scheduling state: the drift register and anything else that decides *where to
# look*. Kept out of the repository so a generated number can never be read back
# as evidence in a report — the firewall notes/2026-08-04-automating-re-analysis.md
# asks for. The weekly workflow keeps its copy as an artifact instead.
scripts/state/
